  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reporting HR: Webinars and an Open Online Course for Journalists</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project addresses the lack of media attention on the issues of human rights, especially in the coverage of crisis events, police action on violators of pandemic measures for example as well as cover of conflict-oriented events, including drug raids and the like. Reports on crime events also fail to consistently point our the lack of due process in police procedures. The webinar is designed to increase the awareness of human rights among journalists and its importance in the democratic scheme, to encourage media to report not just on human rights violations, and to develop a contextual approach as part of the news agenda. Human rights have been absent even in reporting cases when there are obvious violations.</narrative>
  </description>
